{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And play.</b> It is always found doubled in this form." "<b>Hole.</b> The mouth or the nose." "<b>Me'orat.</b> The eye, which is the possessor of light." "It is possible that the heh of <b>ha'dah</b> stands in place of the yod of ידו (his hand), like ידו אליה (Jeremiah 50:14), and the meaning is 'he will stretch out his hand'; or it has no cognate."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:27.364831435Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}